<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54833" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταπλέκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>entwine, plait</i>, [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλοῦν</span>] <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορμοῦ τρόπον
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.98
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> in Anatomy, 
				Pass.
			, perh. <i>inosculate, anastomose</i>, in aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-επλάκην</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Oss.</u>
				18
			</span></i> (aor.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πλεκεῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			); also, <i>to be entwined, matted</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.88
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<i>twine round</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ εὐώνυμα μέρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Meno
					<u>Iatr.</u>
					16.16
				</span></i>
			; <i>compose</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὄσχεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					6.63
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>implicate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τινὰ προδοσίῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.128
				</span></i>
			 (as v.l.):—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος . . καταπεπλεγμένος τῇ
				ποικιλίᾳ</span> in the variety of its events,
				<i>complicated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1459a34
			</span></i>; <i>to be involved</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τούτῳ ψεῦδος κατεπέπλεκτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					2.71
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. dat. pers.,
				<i>entangle, involve in contradictions,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1673.20
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				903.35
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>finish twining</i>: hence metaph., <i>bring to an end</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ζόην, τὴν ῥῆσιν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.205
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.83
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
